# PCI Redaction – IaC Build & Deployment Runbook

## 1. Purpose

This document outlines the step-by-step process for deploying PCI Redaction infrastructure and application components into higher environments.

This runbook is intended for the SRE team to perform infrastructure provisioning and application deployments across environments, including RC and PROD.

It covers:
- Redaction database creation in MS RDS.
- Database user creation and AWS Secrets Manager integration.
- RDS Proxy access configuration.
- Glue VPC endpoint security group updates.
- PCI Redaction infrastructure provisioning through Harness IaC pipelines.
- Lambda and Glue application deployments using the master deployment pipeline.
- S3 event notification configuration for the scanning Lambda.

## 2. Deployment Prerequisites

Before starting the deployment, ensure the following are available:

- Access to the respective Harness project and pipelines.
- Environment-specific Harness input sets.
- Required AWS account and environment access.
- Approved Lambda and Glue image tags.
- Required permissions to perform manual AWS configuration activities.
- Relevant pipeline links and deployment approvals.

